+# Progress: SPEC.md -> todo.js
+
+Goal: implement SPEC.md in todo.js until every check in features.json passes.
+
+## How to check
+Run every `check` in features.json with bash from the repo root (exit 0 = pass). Each check uses a temp copy, so the repo's todos.json is never touched.
+Check-integrity hash (sha256 of JSON.stringify of the list of `check` strings): `4fbf84442cd8b2fea3f35f0977b4710452302375c51e5308a5235ea368756daa`
+
+## Rules
+- Do not edit `check` fields, SPEC.md or the fixture todos.json. Only flip `passes` after the check passes on the latest edit of todo.js.
+- Call something blocked only after it stays the same for 3 rounds; then record it under Blocked and go on to the next feature.
+- No force-push, no history rewrites.
+
+## Status (baseline 2026-11-11, commit 9021c9d, no todo.js yet)
+- 0/4 passing: F1, F2, F3, F4 all FAIL.
+
+## Log
+<!-- one line per round: commit sha, N/4 passing, what changed -->
+
+## Blocked
+<!-- none -->
+
+## Open spec questions (not checked; decide and note here)
+- How `list` behaves with no todos (checks don't cover it).
+- How `done` handles an out-of-range or non-numeric index (checks don't cover it).
+- The todos.json item shape (strings or objects). Checks accept either.
